@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+# Sampled U-filter opportunity diagnostic
+
+This experimental derivative starts from exact dominance profiler `a2dcf8870c17e7edeccb472b27bee0e544eec997`, whose algorithm source is selected correction-on `9d64b7c53ddaea7a578d247ebd28db43ae0d4e56`. We add sampled rejection-coverage measurements. We do not skip labels or change arithmetic, query order, bucket contents, correction, retirement or sorting. The original a2dc worktree, its profiler helpers and active experiment outputs remain separate.
+
+## Build and activation
+
+The new CMake option `KAYROS_U_FILTER_OPPORTUNITY_PROFILING` defaults to `OFF` and requires `KAYROS_DOMINANCE_PROFILING=ON`. Both definitions are public on `lera` to preserve library and bridge layouts. The independent `_core` and its ILS implementation receive neither definition. With the new option disabled and dominance profiling enabled, all 7 checked source/header token streams match a2dc. With both options disabled, the original 6 selected9d OFF equivalence checks also pass.
+
+The runtime opt-in stays `KAYROS_DOMINANCE_PROFILE`, naming a new exclusive JSONL path. The existing `KAYROS_DOMINANCE_PROFILE_STRIDE` and `KAYROS_DOMINANCE_PROFILE_OFFSET` keep defaults `1009` and `0`, with the same independent call sampling per direction, operation and pricing call. The new schema is `kayros-ms58-u-filter-opportunity-v1`, with explicit parent-source and opportunity metadata on every record. Existing a2dc parsers must not be reused silently for this schema.
+
+No mask snapshot is built for an unsampled episode or without runtime opt-in. Every sampled dominance/correction episode has a `sampled_u_filter_opportunity` aggregate under its final survived/eliminated outcome. Merge maintenance receives no opportunity samples. The enclosing native status, returned/unfinished pricing semantics, exclusive output and counters remain those of the parent profiler. An unmatched pricing begin remains unfinished.
+
+The new measurements perturb sampled call timing, including mask construction and per-test accounting. Their timing fields must not be compared to a2dc timings. We do not measure production mask maintenance costs or claim a runtime benefit from ideal rejection coverage.
+
+## Certificates and full snapshot groups
+
+We construct a snapshot only after the existing demand check admits a bucket. Every label currently in that bucket belongs to the snapshot, including cost-ineligible labels, labels that fail individual U tests, and suffixes that the real loop will never reach. We compute separate certificates for the whole bucket and contiguous entry-order blocks of 16, 32 and 64 labels. Each final short block includes its complete tail. Empty buckets are counted explicitly and create no group or vacuous rejection certificate.
+
+For ordinary dominance, a prospective dominator must satisfy `U(m) ⊆ U(l)`. A group's intersection mask `A = AND U(m)` rejects the entire group when `A ⊄ U(l)`. For correction, the arriving label must satisfy `U(m) ⊆ U(l)` for a stored label `l`. A group's union mask `O = OR U(l)` rejects the entire group when `U(m) ⊄ O`. These are sufficient group-rejection certificates, so high individual rejection alone does not guarantee high group rejection.
+
+Masks and original pointer membership remain fixed throughout the bucket scan. Correction visits use a separate monotonically increasing entry ordinal, advanced before any cost check, subset check, continuation or retirement. They never use the shrinking vector index `j` for block membership. Erasures preserve the order of the remaining entries, and sorting occurs after the scan. Snapshot OR masks retain retired members. Their extra bits can weaken a rejection certificate but cannot create a false rejection. Labels retain ownership until cleanup and their U sets are immutable after insertion.
+
+## Counts and interpretation
+
+Each scale records the following quantities independently.
+
+- `snapshot_groups`, `snapshot_members`, `mask_rejected_groups` and `mask_rejected_snapshot_members` describe the full prospective groups, including groups never reached by the original execution.
+- `loop_reached_groups` and `loop_entries` count actual loop entries, including a label that triggers the existing cost break.
+- `u_test_reached_groups` and `actual_u_tests` count groups and labels that reach the real, unrelaxed subset test after the cost check.
+- `subset_pass` and `subset_reject` partition actual U tests in those same sampled episodes.
+- `covered_actual_rejects` counts actual rejected U tests whose full snapshot group has a rejection certificate. This is the numerator for rejection coverage. Divide by `actual_u_tests` for opportunity among actual tests, or by `subset_reject` for coverage among actual rejections. Do not use the parent profiler's unsampled-inclusive counters as a denominator.
+- `cost_break_entries` records the terminating loop-entry label separately. It receives zero actual-U-test or rejection-coverage credit.
+- `retired_members` records real retirement in the original membership, and `certificate_violations` counts a certified group that nevertheless has an actual subset pass.
+
+The 4 granularities overlap and must not be summed. Snapshot group populations are not avoided-label estimates. Credit is restricted to the tests that the original execution actually performs before an early elimination, cost break or return. Early elimination leaves later groups and buckets without coverage credit. Skipping a block containing the existing cost break could change later traversal overhead, so coverage is not a predicted net number of loop visits or a runtime estimate.
+
+The enclosing counters expose `sampled_calls`, bucket entries, demand-break buckets, U-relaxed buckets, full bucket snapshots, empty snapshots, `snapshot_label_reads`, finished snapshots, cost-break snapshots, early-elimination snapshots, unvisited snapshot members and actual retirements. Construction traverses `snapshot_label_reads` distinct labels per snapshot pass and accumulates masks at each of the 4 scales. These counts make otherwise hidden full-bucket construction work visible, including unvisited suffixes. They do not measure the cost of maintaining cached masks in a real algorithm.
+
+U-relaxed episodes construct no masks. Depot shortcuts and the correction cost-relaxation shortcut likewise construct none. The flags `u_relaxed_calls`, `depot_shortcut_calls` and `cost_relaxed_correction_calls` can overlap and are not a disjoint partition of sampled calls. Demand-breaking buckets receive no mask snapshot.
+
+Before using a measurement, require zero `membership_violations`, zero per-scale `certificate_violations`, `subset_pass + subset_reject == actual_u_tests`, and `covered_actual_rejects <= subset_reject` for each scale and scope. These identities are checked in the native fixtures. Interrupted operation episodes are not merged into completed outcomes, as in a2dc, so an unfinished pricing snapshot remains censored.
+
+## Local validation and reserved-node gates
+
+The standalone fixture checks full masks rather than visited-prefix masks, unvisited suffixes, 65-label tails, cost-break-only groups, early elimination, start/middle erasure with fixed entry blocks, conservative stale OR masks, empty buckets, inactive snapshots, deliberately injected membership/certificate violations, sample-only collection, pricing reset and outcome aggregation.
+
+The native fixture exercises 20 scenarios across both arithmetic modes. It checks start/middle retirement, whole-bucket and block coverage, tails, early cost breaks, an early dominator, U-relaxed ordinary/correction calls, the HC correction shortcut, depot bypass, unsampled calls, empty buckets and demand breaks. All real certificate and membership violation counters are zero. Its recorded label states match the a2dc native library with digest `bdbf2a6cabb793c3`. The original correction invariants pass, including both sorting settings. The existing accounting, 5,040-case PWL and native dominance/correction fixtures also pass against the new library.
+
+The local CPLEX static library and `_lera` bridge compile in the project Nix shell. Before any routing pilot, rebuild on reserved compute and rerun these fixtures against the new reserved-node library. The parent comparison must link its separately built a2dc library. Do not reuse the local Nix `.so` on Grid'5000.
+
+```bash
+# Configure on the reserved node with its usual compiler, Boost and CPLEX setup.
+cmake -S . -B build/cplex -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DLERA_LP_BACKEND=cplex -DKAYROS_DOMINANCE_PROFILING=ON -DKAYROS_U_FILTER_OPPORTUNITY_PROFILING=ON -Dpybind11_DIR="$(python -m pybind11 --cmakedir)"
+cmake --build build/cplex --target _lera -j 4
+
+COMMON=(-std=c++23 -O2 -DNDEBUG -ffp-contract=off -DKAYROS_DOMINANCE_PROFILING=1 -DKAYROS_U_FILTER_OPPORTUNITY_PROFILING=1 -Icpp/lera/main/include -Icpp/lera/goc/include -Icpp/lera/nyr/include -Icpp/lera/magic_enum/include)
+g++ "${COMMON[@]}" tests/cpp/test_u_filter_opportunity.cpp -o build/test_u_filter_opportunity
+build/test_u_filter_opportunity
+g++ "${COMMON[@]}" tests/cpp/test_u_filter_opportunity_labeling.cpp build/cplex/cpp/lera/liblera.a -lboost_graph -ldl -lm -o build/test_u_filter_opportunity_labeling
+build/test_u_filter_opportunity_labeling
+```
+
+Use the compiler and library paths from the actual CMake cache. Add its Boost include/library paths when the module environment requires them. The parent differential build uses the same native fixture source and common flags with `KAYROS_U_FILTER_OPPORTUNITY_PROFILING` omitted, linked to a2dc's CPLEX `liblera.a`. Its final state digest must match. Retain compile/run stdout, stderr, exit status, source, library, binary and harness hashes, including failed gates.
+
+No routing experiment has been launched from this worktree, and no runtime or full solver-trajectory equivalence claim is made. Future routing pilots remain restricted to Dabia2013 n25/n50/n100 and CPLEX, with fixed minimalLera `f2c9e20`. The immediate diagnostic control is the original a2dc/selected9d source as appropriate to the question being measured.
